From: Carolina Jubran <cjubran@nvidia.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:01:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net/mlx5e: Avoid WARN_ON when configuring MQPRIO with HTB
 offload enabled

commit 689805dcc474c2accb5cffbbcea1c06ee4a54570 upstream.

[ Backport: 6.1 tc_mqprio_qopt_offload has no extack; report the message with netdev_err() ]

When attempting to enable MQPRIO while HTB offload is already
configured, the driver currently returns `-EINVAL` and triggers a
`WARN_ON`, leading to an unnecessary call trace.

Update the code to handle this case more gracefully by returning
`-EOPNOTSUPP` instead, while also providing a helpful user message.

Signed-off-by: Carolina Jubran <cjubran@nvidia.com>
Reviewed-by: Yael Chemla <ychemla@nvidia.com>
Reviewed-by: Cosmin Ratiu <cratiu@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Tariq Toukan <tariqt@nvidia.com>
Reviewed-by: Kalesh AP <kalesh-anakkur.purayil@broadcom.com>
Signed-off-by: Paolo Abeni <pabeni@redhat.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en_main.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en_main.c
index fb126c7e40c5..4cf73fa4d7a4 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en_main.c
@@ -3539,8 +3539,11 @@ static int mlx5e_setup_tc_mqprio(struct mlx5e_priv *priv,
 	/* MQPRIO is another toplevel qdisc that can't be attached
 	 * simultaneously with the offloaded HTB.
 	 */
-	if (WARN_ON(mlx5e_selq_is_htb_enabled(&priv->selq)))
-		return -EINVAL;
+	if (mlx5e_selq_is_htb_enabled(&priv->selq)) {
+		netdev_err(priv->netdev,
+			   "MQPRIO cannot be configured when HTB offload is enabled.\n");
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+	}
 
 	switch (mqprio->mode) {
 	case TC_MQPRIO_MODE_DCB:
